WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:01.280
- Welcome back, everybody.

00:00:01.280 --> 00:00:03.829
Our next guest has blown
my mind once already

00:00:03.829 --> 00:00:04.966
on our show.

00:00:04.966 --> 00:00:06.490
He's been described by
"The New York Times"

00:00:06.490 --> 00:00:09.840
as having the effervescent wit
of a good dinner party host

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:12.080
and the cunning of a master jewel thief,

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:13.851
which is a really good description.

00:00:13.851 --> 00:00:15.851
His hit off Broadway show is called

00:00:15.851 --> 00:00:17.468
"Asi Wind's Inner Circle".

00:00:17.468 --> 00:00:19.659
Let's say hi to Asi Wind again, everybody.

00:00:19.659 --> 00:00:20.771
(crowd cheering)

00:00:20.771 --> 00:00:23.188
(soft music)

00:00:32.458 --> 00:00:34.147
What's going on?

00:00:34.147 --> 00:00:35.024
- Keeping busy.

00:00:35.024 --> 00:00:36.837
- I am very excited you're here.

00:00:36.837 --> 00:00:37.877
You know I love magic.

00:00:37.877 --> 00:00:38.710
I'm very excited.

00:00:38.710 --> 00:00:39.543
How's your show going?

00:00:39.543 --> 00:00:40.376
- It's going great.

00:00:40.376 --> 00:00:41.209
- [Kelly] Yeah?

00:00:41.209 --> 00:00:42.042
- I mean, we started the show.

00:00:42.042 --> 00:00:42.875
We thought we were gonna
do a couple of months

00:00:42.875 --> 00:00:45.897
and leave and pack, and
we extended six times.

00:00:45.897 --> 00:00:48.680
We've done 370 shows to date.

00:00:48.680 --> 00:00:49.513
(crowd cheering)

00:00:49.513 --> 00:00:51.437
- That's cause you're so awesome.

00:00:51.437 --> 00:00:52.376
It's cause you're so good.

00:00:52.376 --> 00:00:53.848
So what are you showing us today?

00:00:53.848 --> 00:00:56.085
- We're going to try something,
it's something to warm up,

00:00:56.085 --> 00:00:57.317
and then the main course, all right?

00:00:57.317 --> 00:00:58.617
- [Kelly] Okay, oh, I like it.

00:00:58.617 --> 00:00:59.456
- Okay, all right.

00:00:59.456 --> 00:01:01.522
Let's stand, and I'll ask everybody here

00:01:01.522 --> 00:01:02.882
to think of a two digit number

00:01:02.882 --> 00:01:05.930
of the last passcode of
your phone, let's say.

00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:06.889
Everybody think of it.

00:01:06.889 --> 00:01:07.722
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:01:07.722 --> 00:01:08.555
- And if you already have a number,

00:01:08.555 --> 00:01:09.388
raise your hand.

00:01:09.388 --> 00:01:10.712
Quick, quick, raise your
hand, raise your hand.

00:01:10.712 --> 00:01:13.362
All right, how about you
with the beautiful jewelry.

00:01:13.362 --> 00:01:14.672
It's a watch, I think.

00:01:14.672 --> 00:01:16.934
Do you have a two digit
in mind of your last?

00:01:16.934 --> 00:01:18.533
Don't say it, think it, okay.

00:01:18.533 --> 00:01:19.799
- Got it.
- [Asi] You did that?

00:01:19.799 --> 00:01:20.632
- Yep.
- Great.

00:01:20.632 --> 00:01:23.034
All right, I, before the show started,

00:01:23.034 --> 00:01:25.386
I wrote the number on this board.

00:01:25.386 --> 00:01:26.219
- No, you didn't.

00:01:26.219 --> 00:01:27.725
- Yeah, yeah, you'll see, it's crazy.

00:01:27.725 --> 00:01:28.584
Okay.

00:01:28.584 --> 00:01:30.034
- You don't know him, right?

00:01:30.034 --> 00:01:31.187
- I do not know him, never met him.

00:01:31.187 --> 00:01:32.232
- No, no, okay, okay, ready?

00:01:32.232 --> 00:01:36.104
- For the first time,
say the number out loud.

00:01:36.104 --> 00:01:37.021
- Two, one.

00:01:38.581 --> 00:01:40.365
- Also known as 21.

00:01:40.365 --> 00:01:41.198
(audience laughing)

00:01:41.198 --> 00:01:42.031
- Valid.

00:01:42.031 --> 00:01:43.064
- We almost had the same
number, that is crazy.

00:01:43.064 --> 00:01:43.897
- Did you really think it?

00:01:43.897 --> 00:01:45.107
- Should I tell you the first two?

00:01:45.107 --> 00:01:46.939
- No, no, no.

00:01:46.939 --> 00:01:47.798
Okay, you ready?

00:01:47.798 --> 00:01:48.631
- Yeah.

00:01:48.631 --> 00:01:49.958
- Do you wanna see it first?

00:01:49.958 --> 00:01:50.945
- I just want everybody to see it.

00:01:50.945 --> 00:01:54.056
There's no way you have a two and a one.

00:01:54.056 --> 00:01:54.889
Well.

00:01:57.575 --> 00:01:58.408
- Exactly.

00:01:58.408 --> 00:02:01.397
(crowd clapping)

00:02:01.397 --> 00:02:03.258
- It's there somewhere.
- Right, correct, right.

00:02:03.258 --> 00:02:05.447
Okay, okay, it's buried in there.

00:02:05.447 --> 00:02:07.776
So, when I wrote this, I
used two types of markers.

00:02:07.776 --> 00:02:09.898
One is permanent, and one is dry erase.

00:02:09.898 --> 00:02:12.599
So for example, if you did
this, it will erase, right?

00:02:12.599 --> 00:02:13.432
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:13.432 --> 00:02:14.447
- If you did here, you wanna try?

00:02:14.447 --> 00:02:16.156
Try that to 95, try this.

00:02:16.156 --> 00:02:17.175
- [Kelly] Okay, let me try.

00:02:17.175 --> 00:02:19.207
- Yeah, or every one of them will erase,

00:02:19.207 --> 00:02:21.666
but one number is permanent.

00:02:21.666 --> 00:02:22.724
You said 21, right?

00:02:22.724 --> 00:02:23.557
- Yes.

00:02:23.557 --> 00:02:24.390
- No way.

00:02:24.390 --> 00:02:26.390
- [Asi] Try to erase 21.

00:02:28.058 --> 00:02:29.415
- Yeah.

00:02:29.415 --> 00:02:31.538
This one was mine, 22.

00:02:31.538 --> 00:02:34.647
- No, no, I wrote 21 really big.

00:02:34.647 --> 00:02:36.039
Look, I'll show you what I mean.

00:02:36.039 --> 00:02:38.667
If I erase everything, but everything.

00:02:38.667 --> 00:02:39.538
- [Kelly] No!

00:02:39.538 --> 00:02:40.406
(audience gasping)

00:02:40.406 --> 00:02:42.134
- This is 21.

00:02:42.134 --> 00:02:45.134
(audience clapping)

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:47.833
So, thank you.

00:02:49.565 --> 00:02:50.735
- You've never met?

00:02:50.735 --> 00:02:52.207
- Never met him before.

00:02:52.207 --> 00:02:53.668
- What the hell?

00:02:53.668 --> 00:02:54.756
- This is the appetizer.

00:02:54.756 --> 00:02:57.986
Let's, let's do something crazy, shall we?

00:02:57.986 --> 00:02:59.378
- That was crazy.

00:02:59.378 --> 00:03:00.367
- Thank you.

00:03:00.367 --> 00:03:01.586
All right, let's do something crazy.

00:03:01.586 --> 00:03:02.419
- Okay.

00:03:02.419 --> 00:03:04.615
- Crazier, so this is 100 numbers.

00:03:04.615 --> 00:03:08.746
We're taking it up a knot,
1,000 pieces of a jigsaw puzzle.

00:03:08.746 --> 00:03:09.935
Now here's the deal,

00:03:09.935 --> 00:03:12.175
every person here would say,
oh maybe they're all the same.

00:03:12.175 --> 00:03:13.863
You're here to verify
that they're different.

00:03:13.863 --> 00:03:15.346
- They are different, yes.

00:03:15.346 --> 00:03:18.167
- [Asi] So grab, mix them
up a bit if you want.

00:03:18.167 --> 00:03:19.000
- [Kelly] Okay, those are different.

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:21.018
- And then pick about five
or so, like this much.

00:03:21.018 --> 00:03:21.851
Not too many.

00:03:21.851 --> 00:03:23.298
- Okay, just like that.

00:03:23.298 --> 00:03:24.498
- Go ahead, like about five, six pieces.

00:03:24.498 --> 00:03:25.847
Yeah, put 'em here, put them
right in the center here.

00:03:25.847 --> 00:03:27.755
And turn them all facing up.

00:03:27.755 --> 00:03:29.148
- [Kelly] Oh up, okay.

00:03:29.148 --> 00:03:30.085
- So we can see them.

00:03:30.085 --> 00:03:32.186
And you're the eyes,
also we'll zoom on it.

00:03:32.186 --> 00:03:34.727
But you'll see, even
these that are very close,

00:03:34.727 --> 00:03:35.560
they're different.

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:36.447
Even that, different.

00:03:36.447 --> 00:03:37.280
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:38.217
- Even the shape, every one of those.

00:03:38.217 --> 00:03:39.418
Can you divide them into two groups?

00:03:39.418 --> 00:03:41.498
Three and three, any way you want.

00:03:41.498 --> 00:03:42.331
Any three.

00:03:42.331 --> 00:03:43.164
- [Kelly] Boo, boo, boo, boo.

00:03:43.164 --> 00:03:45.187
- Okay, which three, either
three, it doesn't matter.

00:03:45.187 --> 00:03:46.020
- [Kelly] These three.

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:46.853
- [Asi] These, can I take these?

00:03:46.853 --> 00:03:47.686
- [Kelly] Sure.

00:03:47.686 --> 00:03:49.508
- All right, so every
choice you make is your own.

00:03:49.508 --> 00:03:50.980
I'm not trying to influence your choice.

00:03:50.980 --> 00:03:51.813
- I know.

00:03:51.813 --> 00:03:55.108
- From these three, look,
one, two, and three.

00:03:55.108 --> 00:03:57.610
Can you pick any two, any two of them?

00:03:57.610 --> 00:03:59.158
It's up to you.

00:03:59.158 --> 00:04:01.548
Any two, and put 'em right,
yeah, put them in the bag.

00:04:01.548 --> 00:04:02.418
That's perfect.

00:04:02.418 --> 00:04:03.580
- I'm so nervous, okay.

00:04:03.580 --> 00:04:04.413
(audience laughing)

00:04:04.413 --> 00:04:05.246
- Don't worry.

00:04:05.246 --> 00:04:06.079
- Okay, okay.

00:04:06.079 --> 00:04:06.912
- Is it fair?

00:04:06.912 --> 00:04:09.565
From 1,000, you chose six, then three.

00:04:09.565 --> 00:04:10.938
You said, get rid of the other three.

00:04:10.938 --> 00:04:12.357
Then I asked you to remove two.

00:04:12.357 --> 00:04:13.190
- Yeah.

00:04:13.190 --> 00:04:14.023
- We're down to one.

00:04:14.023 --> 00:04:14.856
- Yes.

00:04:14.856 --> 00:04:15.807
- I knew you were going
to choose this one.

00:04:15.807 --> 00:04:16.640
- [Kelly] Why?

00:04:16.640 --> 00:04:17.473
- I'll explain.

00:04:17.473 --> 00:04:19.783
I have the exact same puzzle at home.

00:04:19.783 --> 00:04:23.167
All night, it was a lot of, I
put all the pieces together.

00:04:23.167 --> 00:04:24.000
- Yeah.

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:25.515
- And I, I didn't have time to finish it.

00:04:25.515 --> 00:04:26.967
I was missing one piece.

00:04:26.967 --> 00:04:27.996
- No.

00:04:27.996 --> 00:04:30.956
- Yeah, yeah, it's right here.

00:04:30.956 --> 00:04:33.956
- You are BSing me right now.

00:04:33.956 --> 00:04:35.298
(audience laughing)

00:04:35.298 --> 00:04:36.855
- It's an image, and
it's missing one piece.

00:04:36.855 --> 00:04:38.895
- How in the world would you
know from me randomly grabbing?

00:04:38.895 --> 00:04:40.133
This is not a part of the show.

00:04:40.133 --> 00:04:40.986
I'm not a part of this.

00:04:40.986 --> 00:04:43.018
You are totally, I wanna remove it.

00:04:43.018 --> 00:04:44.155
- It's up to you.

00:04:44.155 --> 00:04:45.066
- Can I look at it?

00:04:45.066 --> 00:04:45.994
- Let's do it together, ready?

00:04:45.994 --> 00:04:46.827
- Okay.

00:04:46.827 --> 00:04:47.660
- Let's just take it off.

00:04:47.660 --> 00:04:48.493
There's one image here.

00:04:48.493 --> 00:04:50.076
- Okay.
- Okay.

00:04:50.076 --> 00:04:51.474
(audience awing)

00:04:51.474 --> 00:04:52.307
- No!

00:04:53.935 --> 00:04:54.852
Oh my gosh!

00:04:56.956 --> 00:04:58.703
(audience laughing and clapping)

00:04:58.703 --> 00:05:00.335
That's my dog!

00:05:00.335 --> 00:05:01.502
I just got it.

00:05:03.834 --> 00:05:05.667
This is my dog, Henry.

00:05:09.334 --> 00:05:11.124
Aw, this is my Henry.

00:05:11.124 --> 00:05:12.103
- It's a gift for you.

00:05:12.103 --> 00:05:16.684
- Oh my gosh, you, I need
to know how you did that.

00:05:16.684 --> 00:05:19.844
You are, this is why it
keeps getting extended.

00:05:19.844 --> 00:05:22.135
I'm so hot right now.

00:05:22.135 --> 00:05:23.724
Oh my God, I'm burning up.

00:05:23.724 --> 00:05:26.071
Okay, give it up for Asi Wind, everybody.

00:05:26.071 --> 00:05:28.074
(audience clapping and cheering)

00:05:28.074 --> 00:05:29.657
That is incredible.

00:05:31.425 --> 00:05:34.034
Be sure to check out
"Asi Wind's Inner Circle"

00:05:34.034 --> 00:05:36.707
at New York's Judson Theater
now through January 14th.

00:05:36.707 --> 00:05:37.540
We will be right back.

